--
N5008 [temp.pre]/1, [basic.pre]/7: `v<E>', an instance of the variable
template `template <long N> constexpr integral_constant<N> v{};', names
an object of class type; initializing an int from it calls the
conversion function on that object.  The front end replaced the
instance by its initializer value, which has no object to call the
conversion function on, and dropped the constructor.  cvise reduction
(/tmp/r163/red/kb_L16span) of libstdc++ 16's span constructor
`span(type_identity_t<element_type> (&)[_ArrayExtent]) : _M_ptr(__arr),
_M_extent(__v<_ArrayExtent>)' (span:201,
cpp11_static_cast_of_array_parameter_to_pointer/test_libstdcxx.desc with
GCC 16's headers).  Fails on bin53.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the
program.
